Z||000075||terryk||12-16-2001||12:09 AM||||Be careful here folks. Those pesky little LT1's have far more torque than a DOHC can ever imagine.<P>Unless your DOHC powered (insert car name here) has actually beat an LT1, don't go talking people into swaps with that expectation.||||reg||13
Z||000076||lowCG||12-16-2001||01:18 AM||||There's not going to be a real good chance of smoking past a newer 330+hp Trans Am or anything,but there are some real sweet spots in the powerband;just think of it as the way they should have been built.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000077||terryk||12-16-2001||12:45 PM||||Exactly. We get some extraordinary claims around here. I wouldn't put any NA DOHC against any LT1 in a drag race. <P>On the otherhand, a DOHC power Fiero is extremely high on grin factor!<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 12-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000078||lowCG||12-16-2001||10:50 PM||||Yeah,I'll walk away from the car sometimes,and turn back to look at it with a big grin;never did that very often before the 3.4 swap.||||reg||14
